# =============================================================================
# Nkanyezi Tours - .gitignore
# CMPG213 Group 6
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR
# ---------------------
# Git tries to track every file in the folder. Most of what Visual Studio
# creates should NOT be tracked: it is rebuilt automatically, it is different on
# every machine, and it is large. Committing it causes merge conflicts that
# cannot be resolved, in files nobody wrote.
#
# If you ever see "bin", "obj" or ".vs" in your list of changes, something is
# wrong with this file - say so in the group chat rather than committing them.
# =============================================================================


# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. Rebuilt every time you press F5. Never commit.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Oo]ut/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Visual Studio's own working folder and per-user settings.
#
# .vs/ holds your window layout, your open tabs and a local database of the
# solution. It is yours alone and is enormous. The .user files hold things like
# which page starts when you press F5.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
*.userprefs

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONNECTION STRINGS AND SECRETS
#
# appsettings.json IS committed, because everyone needs the same structure.
# appsettings.Development.json is NOT, because that is where you put your own
# server name if yours is not localhost\SQLEXPRESS.
#
# Rule: no password, no connection string with a password in it, and no API key
# ever goes into a file that is committed. If you commit one by accident, tell
# Reinhardt immediately - deleting it in a later commit does not remove it from
# the history.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json
secrets.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NuGet packages. Restored automatically from the .csproj, so there is no reason
# to commit hundreds of megabytes of them.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
packages/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
project.lock.json
project.fragment.lock.json
artifacts/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ASP.NET / web specific
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
wwwroot/dist/
node_modules/
*.publishsettings
PublishProfiles/
*.pubxml
*.pubxml.user
*.azurePubxml

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SQL Server local database files.
#
# The database itself is NOT in git. The .sql scripts are. Everyone rebuilds
# their own copy by running 01-schema.sql and 03-seed-data.sql. That is the
# whole reason those files are numbered.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.mdf
*.ldf
*.ndf
*.bak
*.dbmdl
*.jfm

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and coverage output
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
[Bb]uild[Ll]og.*
*.coverage
*.coveragexml
*.trx

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ReSharper / Rider, if anyone uses them
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
_ReSharper*/
*.[Rr]e[Ss]harper
.idea/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operating system clutter
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Office lock files.
#
# When somebody has a Word document open, Word creates a hidden ~$ file next to
# it. Committing those causes confusing conflicts on the submission documents.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$*
*.tmp
*~

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Draw.io backups
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.drawio.bkp
*.drawio.dtmp
